# Cache-Control for Netlify and Cloudflare Pages. Ignored by GitHub Pages, which
# sets its own headers — harmless there, so it costs nothing to carry.
#
# The rule is: anything whose name can change gets a year, anything whose name
# cannot gets revalidated. Fonts, images and the favicon are content that only
# ever changes by being replaced with a differently-named file, so a year is
# safe. styles.css and main.js keep their names across deploys, so they get
# no-cache — which does not mean "do not cache", it means "ask first": the
# browser keeps the file and revalidates, and an unchanged file comes back as a
# 304 with no body. HTML is the same, so a copy fix is live immediately.
#
# If a build step ever adds content hashes to the CSS and JS filenames, move
# those two into the year bucket. Until then this is the correct trade.

/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
